Place the handset on the base station to  charge the handset. When the handset is  placed correctly on the base station, you hear a  docking sound.  ->  The handset starts charging.

<PIC:Manual22_27>
{{image description: Blue note icon with three white horizontal lines and the word Note.}}

The battery icon displays the current battery

<PIC:Manual22_28>
{{image description: Diagram of the handset on the base station with a magnified battery-level icon showing stacked battery bars on the display.}}

The handset turns off if the batteries are empty.  If you are on the phone, you hear warning  tones when the batteries are almost empty. The  call gets disconnected after the warning.

<PIC:Manual22_29>
{{image description: Battery icon explanation panel. It shows full, medium, low, and empty battery icons and text explaining that bars indicate battery level off the charger, scroll while charging, and an empty icon flashes when the battery is low.}}

#### Display icons

