<PIC:Manual22_47>
{{image description: Note callout icon with a blue square containing white horizontal lines and the word Note beside it on a mostly blank page.}}

To join an external call with another handset, press the Talk key.

<PIC:Manual22_48>
{{image description: Note callout icon with a blue square containing white horizontal lines and the word Note beside it.}}

There are two ways to block incoming calls:
- block anonymous calls;
- create a blacklist.

<PIC:Manual22_49>
{{image description: Standalone blue note icon with three white horizontal lines on a mostly blank page.}}

This feature checks and formats your outgoing  call number before it is dialed out. The prefix  number can replace the detect number you  set in the menu. For example, you set 604 as  the detect number and 1250 as the prefix.  When you have dialed out a number such as  6043338888, your phone changes the number  to 12503338888 when it dials out.

